+# Companion timer for survive-supervisor.service -- WAKES every 2 hours.
+# A wake does ONE thing per citizen: execute a finished decision, or else author
+# a new mission (survive-supervisor.js main(): the loop `continue`s after an
+# execution). So a mission is authored on one wake and executed on the next:
+# about ONE MISSION EVERY 4 HOURS (~6 a day, strictly alternating author /
+# execute in bus/survive-supervisor.log), not every 2. MISSION_COOLDOWN_HOURS=2
+# is measured from the last mission-resolved, which is written at execution time,
+# so it is satisfied by exactly one timer interval. Consequence: a decision waits
+# up to 2h after it is written before it is executed.
